SUMMARY:Death Valley — MLK weekend\, January 2027
LOCATION:Echo Canyon Road\, site E1\, Death Valley National Park
GEO:36.4617;-116.796
DESCRIPTION:Three nights camped on our own gravel pad off Echo Canyon Road\, a few miles from Furnace Creek\, in the one season when Death Valley is comfortable: sunny 60s by day\, dark skies and cold\, silent nights. The lowest\, hottest\, driest place in North America is at its best in January — and there is room at camp for more people.\\nhttps://aaronmsoto.github.io/travel-guides/guides/death-valley/
